ROLE: prose. ONE iteration. You are unattended; nobody will answer questions.

Do exactly one unit of work, commit it, push it, and stop. A wrapper script
relaunches you. Do not loop inside this run. Do not try to finish the book in
one pass.

FIRST, orient (cheap, do it every time — the repo moves between runs):
  git fetch origin --prune
  git show origin/planning/kanban-automation:handoff/AUTONOMOUS_LOOP.md
  python3 scripts/generate_status.py

Book 1 lives ONLY on origin/expand/book1-ch01-10. Every other branch is 41,000
words short. The pipeline scripts live only on main. Work from main and read
chapters across with `git show`; commit manuscript changes to the expand branch.

GET THE WORK LIST FROM THE REPO, NOT FROM THIS PROMPT:

  bash loop/done.sh

It prints the five worst chapters against their targets in
books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/EXPANSION_TRACKER.md. Take the worst one.
Targets live in that tracker -- never hardcode one from memory or from an
earlier message. An earlier draft of this prompt carried hand-copied targets
and every one of them was wrong.

Scale of the job, so you do not mistake progress for completion: the book is
at 101,298 of 187,000 words. All 33 chapters are under target. The shortfall
is ~86,000 words. At one chapter per iteration this is a long run, and that
is expected -- do not batch chapters to go faster.

After the word targets, in order:
  - deadpan-reply tic at emotional peaks: ch20, 24, 25, 29, 32
  - continuity: Dr. Amara Park (B2 ch2) -> Lian Park; Leela Sen -> Leela Nair;
    Dr. Lian Zhou (B2 ch27) collides with Book 1's Lian Park

ONE chapter per iteration, all six passes before you mark it done.

THE SIX-PASS SOURCES -- exact paths, all three verified to exist. Each lives
on a DIFFERENT branch, so read them with git show, not cat:

  git show origin/planning/kanban-automation:planning/BSBC_PASS6.md
  git show origin/expand/book1-ch01-10:books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/\
CLAUDE_BSBC_FINAL_REVIEW.md
  git show origin/expand/book1-ch01-10:books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/\
EXPANSION_TRACKER.md          # the Rules section is binding on every expansion

BOOK 1 IS NOT BOOK 2. These files exist ONLY for Book 2 -- do not go looking
for a Book 1 copy and do not create one:
  START_HERE.md            (Book 2 only -- Book 1 has no equivalent)
  CHAPTER_ATTESTATIONS.md  (Book 2 only)

Book 1 tracks state in EXPANSION_TRACKER.md ("Expansion status" column) and
STATE_LEDGER.md. Update the tracker row in the same commit as the chapter.
Do not create a new tracking file -- this book already has eleven.

EXPANSION MEANS SCENES, NOT SENTENCES. If word count rises because paragraphs
got longer, the density pass failed. Convert summary into scene. The reference
repair is ch31 (2,328 -> 3,650): it gave a seventeen-year reunion room to
happen and answered a question the previous draft deferred to a sequel. Read
that diff before your first expansion.

STOP THE LOOP (write loop/STOP and say why) if:
  - a destructive git operation would be needed
  - a canon decision is required (names, cutting a chapter, what the countdown
    counts toward)
  - the same check fails three times with different fixes attempted

Commit message: say what you LEARNED, not only what changed. Then exit.
